mission.","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 48b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_48b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Mekhilta DeRabbi Yishmael, Tractate Pischa 16:22","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mekhilta_DeRabbi_Yishmael%2C_Tractate_Pischa_16.22"},"witness":"Beeri Edition, Koren, Jerusalem, 2019"}]},{"raw":"נ\"ל שצ\"ל א\"ר חסדא אמר רב","reason":"The checked Sanhedrin gives Rav Chisda alone first. Preserve the added Rav as a voiced emendation.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 69b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_69b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"דר' חייא בר נחמני צ\"ל א\"ר חייא בריה דרבה בר נחמני","reason":"Avodah Zarah 31a and 49b carry the two different forms. Heilprin’s emendation and argument are distinct from either received reading.","evidence":[{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 31a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_31a.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 49b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_49b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"ושם (ס' סע\"ב) א\"ר חייא בריה דאבא (צ\"ל דרבה)","reason":"The exact Avodah Zarah witness carries Abba. Heilprin proposes Rabbah here and does so separately in Berakhot.","evidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 43a:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_43a.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 60b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_60b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"אבא בר חם פי' רב צמח גאון בר פלטויה בערוך שלו","reason":"The checked Bavli passages supply Chama and Chanan. The Yuchasin wording and the cited Arukh attribution remain unsettled.","evidence":[{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 31a:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zar